            <div class="main-content">
                <h2>Achieve Clear, Confident Skin</h2>
                <p>Acne affects nearly 85% of people at some point in their lives. Whether you're a teenager dealing with breakouts or an adult struggling with persistent acne, our board-certified dermatologists offer advanced treatments that go beyond over-the-counter solutions.</p>
                
                <h3>Why Professional Acne Treatment?</h3>
                <p>While drugstore products can help mild acne, many cases require prescription-strength treatments. Professional care offers:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Accurate diagnosis of your specific acne type</li>
                    <li>Access to prescription medications not available OTC</li>
                    <li>Treatment of hormonal factors</li>
                    <li>Prevention of permanent scarring</li>
                    <li>Faster, more effective results</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h3>Types of Acne We Treat</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Comedonal Acne:</strong> Blackheads and whiteheads from clogged pores</li>
                    <li><strong>Inflammatory Acne:</strong> Red, swollen papules and pustules</li>
                    <li><strong>Cystic Acne:</strong> Deep, painful nodules and cysts</li>
                    <li><strong>Hormonal Acne:</strong> Breakouts related to hormonal fluctuations</li>
                    <li><strong>Adult Acne:</strong> Acne persisting into or starting in adulthood</li>
                    <li><strong>Back & Body Acne:</strong> Acne on the chest, back, and shoulders</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h3>Our Treatment Options</h3>
                <p>We customize treatment based on your acne type, severity, and individual factors:</p>
                
                <h4>Topical Treatments</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Prescription retinoids (tretinoin, adapalene, tazarotene)</li>
                    <li>Topical antibiotics</li>
                    <li>Benzoyl peroxide preparations</li>
                    <li>Combination therapies</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h4>Oral Medications</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Oral antibiotics for inflammatory acne</li>
                    <li>Hormonal treatments (birth control pills, spironolactone)</li>
                    <li>Isotretinoin (Accutane) for severe, treatment-resistant acne</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h4>In-Office Procedures</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Chemical peels to unclog pores and reduce inflammation</li>
                    <li>Professional extractions</li>
                    <li>Cortisone injections for cystic acne</li>
                    <li>Light and laser therapy</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h3>Acne Scar Treatment</h3>
                <p>If acne has left scars, we offer treatments to improve skin texture:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Microneedling to stimulate collagen production</li>
                    <li>Chemical peels for surface irregularities</li>
                    <li>Laser resurfacing for deeper scars</li>
                    <li>Dermal fillers for depressed scars</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h3>What to Expect</h3>
                <p>During your consultation, we will:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Evaluate your skin and acne type</li>
                    <li>Discuss your medical history and previous treatments</li>
                    <li>Identify potential contributing factors</li>
                    <li>Create a personalized treatment plan</li>
                    <li>Provide guidance on proper skincare routines</li>
                    <li>Schedule follow-ups to monitor progress</li>
                </ul>
